lises", "01": "urban areas", "10": "cityscapes", "11": "towns"}}, {"for": {"0": "for", "1": "for"}}, {"future": {"00": "coming", "01": "ensuing", "10": "subsequent", "11": "prospective"}}, {"generations": {"00": "lineages", "01": "progenies", "10": "offspring", "11": "descendants"}}], "container": "Urbanization refers to the rapid growth and expansion of cities, resulting in the increased population and development of urban areas. This phenomenon has had a profound impact on society, both positive and negative. One of the major effects of urbanization is the economic growth and development it brings. Urban areas attract more businesses and industries, leading to job opportunities and increased income for the population. This, in turn, has improved the standard of living for many people. Additionally, urbanization has promoted innovation and technological advancements, as cities become centers for research and development. However, urbanization has also led to several negative consequences. One such effect is the strain on infrastructure and resources. With the influx of people, cities often face challenges in providing essential services such as housing, transportation, and sanitation. This can result in overcrowding, traffic congestion, and inadequate access to basic amenities. Moreover, urbanization has contributed to the deterioration of the environment. The expansion of cities often leads to deforestation, pollution, and the destruction of natural habitats. This poses significant threats to biodiversity and exacerbates climate change. In conclusion, urbanization has had both positive and negative effects on society. While it has contributed to economic growth and development, it has also placed strain on infrastructure and the environment. It is essential for policymakers and urban planners to address these challenges effectively to ensure sustainable and inclusive cities for future generations.", "encoded_message": "Metropolitanization signifies to the swift development and enlargement of urban centers, leading in the amplified residents and progress of municipal localities. The event has had a deep bearing on community, both beneficial and harmful. A single of the main outcomes of urbanization is the financial growth and development it generates. Urban areas pull in more enterprises and areas, engendering to work options and increased earnings for the population. This, in turn, has upgraded the quality of life for a multitude of people. Additionally, urbanization has stimulated creativity and tech progress, as cities evolve into nuclei for study and progression. But, urbanization has also brought about to a number of harmful outcomes. A comparable influence is the pressure on structure and assets. With the inflow of inhabitants, municipalities regularly meet issues in furnishing necessary amenities akin as lodging, transit, and cleanliness. This can bring about in crowding, traffic congestion, and inadequate access to basic amenities. Moreover, urbanization has contributed to the deterioration of the environment. The expansion of cities often leads to deforestation, pollution, and the destruction of natural habitats. This poses significant threats to biodiversity and exacerbates climate change. In conclusion, urbanization has had both positive and negative effects on society. While it has contributed to economic growth and development, it has also placed strain on infrastructure and the environment. It is essential for policymakers and urban planners to address these challenges effectively to ensure sustainable and inclusive cities for future generations.", "encoding_time_report": {"container_generation": 21.06, "secret_key_generation": 49.34}, "decoding_time": 0.0008289813995361328, "decoded_message": "00110010001100100101011101010010000111011010011111010110110001001011111110000100100000111101101001010100011010111000101101101101", "error_message": ""}